{"questions":[{"question_id":"07XXSkPNgWGKLYw1","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2011","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"chemical-equilibrium","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"chemical-equilibrium-law-of-mass-action-and-equilibrium-constant","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"a-vessel-at-1000-k-contains-co2-with-a-pressure-of-05-atm-2011-marks-4-07xxskpngwgklyw1.htm","content":"A vessel at 1000 K contains CO<sub>2</sub> with a pressure of 0.5 atm. Some of the CO<sub>2</sub> is converted into CO on\nthe addition of graphite. If the total pressure at equilibrium is 0.8 atm, the value of K is :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"3 atm "},{"identifier":"B","content":"0.3 atm "},{"identifier":"C","content":"0.18 atm"},{"identifier":"D","content":"1.8 atm "}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>To determine the equilibrium constant <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.011ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 889 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, consider the equilibrium reaction: </p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.532ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"30.123ex\" height=\"2.229ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 13314.6 985.4\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"